me zero-argument samples. MEASURED 2026-10-01, 3.12.3, whole product (151 units), --all: 40 builtins (METH_O + METH_FASTCALL), 81 positions, 37 with a never type, 2 over budget (compile); signature 48 agree / 9 differ — every one a METH_FASTCALL\\|METH_KEYWORDS builtin whose missing argument goes through _PyArg_UnpackKeywords (the keyword parser, not resolved: content) — / 24 without a signature; witness 837 confirmed / 0 contradicted; facts 107 s + readings 389 s, 6.3 GB. Exact readings: len (the 8 sized types), abs (int, bool, float, complex), chr / bin (int, bool), getattr / hasattr / delattr's name (str only), callable (always). ⚠ the str / bytes / list representatives are EMPTY (ord's are never: ord('') raises); a returned NEW object is an allocation's unknown result, so most accepted types read content, not always. CART-1258 |\n","file":".claude/skills/cartograph/references/questions.md"}},"verb":"edit"}],"explained":72721,"commit":"a36b560edf40ce0c6fb47f458e9c343f3a1f7f4a","hand":0,"open_intents":[],"entries":[{"decided_by":"tactic","decisions":[],"verb":"edit","invocation":{"verb":"edit","touched":["lua/cartograph/cinterp/facts/compdb-make.lua"],"args":{"before":"        local compiles, links\n        for _, extra in ipairs({ {}, { '-B' } }) do\n            local cmd = { 'make', '-n' }\n            vim.list_extend(cmd, extra)\n            local r = vim.system(cmd, { cwd = src, text = true, env = env }):wait(300000)\n            compiles, links = parse((r.stdout or '') .. '\\n' .. (r.stderr or ''), src)\n            if #compiles > 0 then break end\n        end\n","file":"lua/cartograph/cinterp/facts/compdb-make.lua","after":"        -- (★ `-B` makes every target out of date — the MAKEFILES too, and GNU make REMAKES a makefile even under `-n`:\n        -- on CPython that re-ran config.status and rewrote the configured tree. Every makefile make reads — the main\n        -- one, each `include` that exists — is held OLD with `-o`)\n        local holds = {}\n     